// SELECT tool: pick / marquee / move / resize / duplicate / delete / group / align.
//
// Design rules (see AGENTS.md + the staging brief):
//  * A drag is a LOCAL PREVIEW (originals hidden, transformed copies painted on the fx layer). Nothing is
//    written to Yjs until the gesture ends, so Escape / a pinch / pointercancel simply drops the preview.
//  * Every committed action is exactly ONE doc.transact(..., session.LOCAL), fenced by undo.stopCapturing()
//    on both sides, so per-device undo/redo treats it as one step and never merges it with a stroke.
//  * Y.Map items are never removed + reinserted to change them: fields are mutated in place. A freehand
//    stroke's points are replaced with m.set('points', new Y.Array) (last-writer-wins on the field) rather
//    than delete+insert inside the old array, so two devices moving the same stroke concurrently can never
//    end up with both point sets concatenated.
//  * Commit re-reads the live Y.Map values and applies the gesture's transform to them, and skips items that
//    another device deleted mid-drag, so remote edits during a drag cannot corrupt state.
//  * Geometry comes from render.js (getEntry/buildEntry/hitEntry), so hit-testing, bounds and drawing agree.
